    },
    {
      "text": "While planning how to obtain divine travel Gu, Fang Yuan ranks Northern Plains’ Imperial court with Southern Border’s Fei clan and Eastern Sea’s Zui Xian Weng among forces that may already hold such wine and thus better odds at that Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        411
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_divine_travel",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "fac_fei_clan",
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "char_zui_xian_weng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In those memories, Hei tribe leader Hei Lou Lan succeeds and becomes the lord of the imperial court for ten years. After two years as lord of the grassland, he is deceived into leaving the imperial court and killed, and the tribes contend again for the ruler of the imperial court.",
      "chapters": [
        427
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lord-of-the-grassland",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_hei_tribe",
        "char_hei_lou_lan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Every ten years northern plains faces a terrifying blizzard. Only by entering the Imperial Court can one have protection from that blizzard. The quota is limited, so tribes battle bitterly, eliminate the weak, and decide the master of the Imperial Court.",
      "chapters": [
        478
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blizzard-refuge-and-quota",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
